	url = {https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85163389072&doi=10.1063%2f5.0140150&partnerID=40&md5=fa24d200cd9ea44e97fdc87613c9e556},
	affiliations = {Information System Program, Mathematics and Information Technology Department, Institut Teknologi Kalimantan, Balikpapan, Indonesia; Digital Business Program, Mathematics and Information Technology Department, Institut Teknologi Kalimantan, Balikpapan, Indonesia},
	abstract = {Potentially, the local goods (snacks and handicrafts) may be the important regional income source of Balikpapan, a city in Kalimantan (East Kalimantan Province). But Balikpapan's local goods have not been known yet by many people who visit the city. Therefore, both marketing and selling digitalization of the local goods is required by developing e-commerce website for the micro, small, and medium-sized enterprises (MSMEs) in order to sell or promote their local products in Balikpapan. In order to develop the e-commerce website, the recommendations of the e-commerce website design are required based on competitive research. The competitive research is viewed based on both perspectives: MSME local entrepreneurs' requirements or expectations analysis to the system and each user/customer's experiences when using the existing e-commerce applications (online shops or marketplaces) in order to capture the prospects of the e-commerce website for MSME local products in Balikpapan. This research was done by both methods: interviewing 5 respondents who are MSME entrepreneurs in Balikpapan and surveying 56 respondents who are the users/customers of existing e-commerce applications in Indonesia by using the questionnaires (they were distributed in both online by using Google Form and offline). The questionnaires for surveying the respondents were designed based on Jakob Nielsen's 10 heuristic principals of usability. The data of respondents' survey was analysed by both Microsoft Excel (respondents' descriptive analysis) and IBM SPSS Statistics 25 (primary analysis, including both data validity and reliability tests). The data of respondents' interview was analysed by NVivo. Based on the partners' perspective generally, they have the positive expectations to the e-commerce website and even, they need a training/workshop about MSME business development strategy on e-commerce platform. Based on each customer's experiences perspective, the customer prefers choosing e-commerce platform due to online shopping is more practical than conventional shopping, getting discount price for the certain products, payment facility of "pay later"is available, and user-friendly features on e-commerce application. On the other hand, only both Match Between System & the Real World and Help User Recognize, Dialogue, & Recover from Errors affect to Usability. Therefore, copywriting aspects (including "good or understandable error message"on an application) are important to be concerned for the e-commerce website design, as a part of the e-commerce website development. But both customer service quality and security/privacy issues need to be concerned when the e-commerce website will have been finished and released officially due to the issues contribute to an e-commerce application's customers retention or loyalty. This research is still on-going research. Even for long term, this research's outcomes (the recommendations) need to continue at development progresses of the e-commerce website until it will have been finished and released officially, then it will be evaluated about its UI/UX design as the users' requirements later (at the next researches).  © 2023 Author(s).},
