	affiliations = {Bina Nusantara University, Entrepreneurship Department, Malang, Indonesia},
	abstract = {Cybercrime is one of the factors that affect consumer confidence in using e-commerce. This phenomenon is evidenced by the case of hacking personal data of e-commerce consumers that occurred in 2022 in Indonesia. This causes consumer confidence in providing their data digitally to decrease, the rise of cases of improper use of personal data in the digital world, especially e-commerce, is one of the reasons this research was written. Therefore, by using the Theory of the Effect of Security and Privacy on Consumer Satisfaction and Trust as the main concept, this research is expected to have a good impact on building e-commerce, especially in Indonesia, to be able to improve data security and safeguarding as a form of consumer privacy in maintaining consumer satisfaction and trust in the use of e-commerce in everyday life. The analysis was conducted on 163 respondents with online distribution with the domicile of the subject spread across Indonesia. The results of this analysis show that consumer satisfaction can be based on the existence of securities and privacy that are maintained, consumer trust also shows the influence of satisfaction and privacy. However, it is found that security does not have a significant impact on trust, as well as satisfaction does not mediate between security and trust and satisfaction partially mediates between privacy and trust. © 2024 IEEE.},
