	affiliations = {Computer Science Department School of Computer Science, Bina Nusantara University, Jakarta, 11480, Indonesia; Research Center for Artificial Intelligence and Cyber Security National Research and Innovation Agency (BRIN), Jakarta, Indonesia},
	abstract = {Online marketplace platforms create opportunities for vendors to sell their products to consumers online. During the early phase of the COVID pandemic, the adoption of online shopping in Indonesia is rapidly increasing. This rising state of online marketplace usage produces abundant data and allows researchers to conduct studies and explore. Product review data in the online marketplace contain rich information for emotion analysis tasks. This research proposes an emotion recognition model using the PRDECT-ID dataset. The TF-IDF approach is utilized as the baseline model for this research. Then, the authors focus on fine-tuning IndoBERT to outperform the baseline model. For the evaluation, the F1-Score was used to evaluate the models’ performance. This research found that the best configuration model is fine-tuned IndoBERT-base-p1 with 3e-6 as the learning rate, 32 for the batch size, and training with four epochs. The F1-Score of fine-tuned IndoBERT is 71%, surpassing the TF-IDF model by 9%. © 2023 IEEE.},
